  Read it like this:
   * NAMELESS% is the size of the screenshot-fallback surface - the number your
     hybrid design has to live with. Judge it on the accessible NAME (own text/desc,
     else child labels), not on the control's own attributes: on stock Settings the
     own-attribute view said 59% anonymous and the name-aware view said 0%.
   * ridX/descX are collisions: a hook exists but is shared, so it needs a
     scoped chain. High collisions mean 'ladder + scoping', not 'no hooks'.
   * rid is version-pinned. Re-run this per app build to get half-life.

